{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple","id":1103407,"title":"Chimerical Beasts in Secrets of The Ruined Temple","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-14T00:37:02-07:00","id":1103407,"title":"Chimerical Beasts in Secrets of The Ruined Temple","content":"Re-reading <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/11922/Secrets-of-the-Ruined-Temple?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</b></a> book for <b>Mage</b>, I found there is probably first mentioning of the Begotten, years before proper gameline ( <b>SotRT</b> is from 2006 year ). It starts on page 120 of book and gives interesting ideas on Beasts to be used in game world. What do you think about those concepts? How would you implement those Chimerical Beasts in the BtP as it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T04:17:17-07:00","id":1103435,"title":"","content":"Interesting passages are only 2-3 paragraphs, so I will cite them below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SotRT, p. 119</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chimerical Beasts </b><br /> The denizens of the Temenos arise from the depths of the human mind. Like the Realms in which they dwell, the beings embody myths, icons, hopes and fears. But unlike Astral Realms, Astral beings can think. They have <i>desires</i>. And not all of them are content to be creatures of other beings\u2019 dreams. Mages call beings that cross from the Temenos to the material world \u201cchimerical beasts,\u201d no matter what their form. Such creatures are rare, to say the least, but they do exist; how and why is a subject furiously dissected by Awakened cryptozoologists.<br /> <br /> Some mages conflate chimerical beasts with cryptids, but while these groups may overlap, accurate categorization is no clear-cut task. The line between a spirit and a chimerical beast is not always easy to draw. The <i>essence</i> of hatred lives in the Shadow Realm, while the <i>idea</i> of hatred exists in Astral Space, but humans can find the distinction tough to grasp when they both manifest in the material world.<br /> <br /> Once physically incarnated, chimerical beasts react in a variety of ways. Unintelligent creatures respond like any animals removed from their natural habitat. Often they seek dark places to hide or lash out violently. Intelligent beasts sometimes scheme to achieve incarnation for years, and have planned extensively for material existence. No encounter with a chimerical beast should be taken lightly \u2014 a being able to endure in the Temenos is a being with the power of an eternal icon.<br /> <br /> <b>Breeds of Beast </b><br /> Chimerical beasts come in many different forms. Often, mages familiar with one type of beast are entirely unaware of others. The spawn of dreams tend not to view themselves as a unified group at all: originating in the Temenos doesn\u2019t link them together any more than originating in the physical world makes humans and hyenas treat each other as brothers.<br /> <br /> <b>Myths</b><br /> Why do so many creatures of myth exist within the Temenos? Did dragons, basilisks, djinn and Nagas once live in the real world, only to fade into memory? Or do stories of monsters create monsters in the human mind, built from the stuff of fear and awe, eventually to manifest in the material world? Either way, monsters <i>do</i> exist in dreams, and monsters <i>do </i>incarnate in reality. Mythological chimerical beasts resemble cryptids in most respects, though the chimerical beasts are more likely than cryptids to reveal themselves to Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Unlike traditional cryptids, chimerical beasts haven\u2019t found ways to hide in the modern world. Unless they know better, they\u2019re likely to treat humans the same way they did in legends. Fortunately, chimerical beasts rarely incarnate in densely populated areas, but nothing prevents a mage from guiding a beast to human prey.<br /> <br /> Mythological beasts often demonstrate \u201caffection\u201d for theculture that first told stories about them. They may hesitate to attack modern representatives of their culture, or they may feel betrayed and angry if men and women from their culture don\u2019 behave according to tradition. (Imagine a dragon that can\u2019t find a better princess to kidnap than the local prom queen, and then becomes furious because no knight will come forth to do battle and rescue her.) They may be drawn to culturally significant locations or population centers, desperately seeking the familiar in anything from religious institutions to museum exhibitions to ethnic restaurants. Even the trappings of a culture can be enough to appease some beasts: a Nigerian mage who does his research may be better prepared to face a hydra than a Greek American mage who ignores her roots.<br /> <br /> Not all beasts care about their origins, of course. The more cross-cultural myths a monster appears in, the less likely it is to feel tied to a particular group. Some monsters are even eager to embrace the modern world and adapt their behavior accordingly: a phoenix might build its nest in the fires of a steel mill, and a troll might kidnap homeless children and carry them to its home in the storm drains.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-14-2017, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T04:22:00-07:00","id":1106479,"title":"","content":"We can always say that the Chimerical beasts are indeed Beasts and their Horrors, and mages just missed the larger cycle of the Primordial Dream; that of fear and hunger.<br /> <br /> I'm more interested about the material incarnation and &quot;hiding in the mortal world&quot; that some of those Chimericals attempt, since as of Mage 2e (and Beast), Goetia can't manifest by themselves in the waking world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:37:24-07:00","id":1106578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1106479#post1106479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more interested about the material incarnation and &quot;hiding in the mortal world&quot; that some of those Chimericals attempt, since as of Mage 2e (and Beast), Goetia can't manifest by themselves in the waking world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking this &quot;hiding in the mortal world&quot; is exactly about Beasts - because, on the day to day basis. Horrors are <i>hidden </i>inside Beasts human body, don't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:15:07-07:00","id":1107064,"title":"","content":"I like the idea! In reality, no, the writers were intending something else entirely---actual Astral spirits!---but, looking back, its <i>awfully</i> easy to retcon Beasts in there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T07:31:53-07:00","id":1108754,"title":"","content":"But are not horrors actual Astral Spirits? The Primordial Dream exists in the Astral... &gt;.&gt;<br /> I'm just making a suggestion that hey.... What if that passage was a piece of Inspiration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 06-28-2017, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T15:51:13-07:00","id":1108987,"title":"","content":"Horrors have never been defined from a mage's perspective, but considering that they're native to the Temenos it's likely they're Goetia (or close to Goetia) instead of spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T13:26:01-07:00","id":1109373,"title":"","content":"Whats the difference between Astral Spirits and Goetia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T13:34:26-07:00","id":1109375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1109373#post1109373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats the difference between Astral Spirits and Goetia?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not that familiar with First Edition, but in Second Edition there is no such thing as an Astral Spirit. <br /> <br /> Goetia are Ephemeral Entites native to the Astral plain. They are created by human minds and have forms based on that; either individuals with their own 'inner demons' or collectivley for popular archetypes. (Beasts are formed from collective fears, thus Goetia is the closest to them)<br /> <br /> Spirits are Ephemeral Entites native to the Shadow. They form from the Resonance of things and emotions of the material plane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T18:03:42-07:00","id":1109513,"title":"","content":"As said Spirits and Goetia are different types of ephemeral entities. The former hangs our in the Shadow and embodies a multitude of concepts in the world, such as objects, animals, feelings and forces. The latter hangs out in the Astral and embodies a multitude of concepts based on people's minds and souls, and Humanity's collective consciousness. If Astral Spirits were to exist they'd presumably be Spirits that for some reason or other hangs out in the Astral. Depending on what concepts they embody they might be indistinguishable from Goetia without supernatural means of checking, but metaphysically speaking they'd be made up of two different types of ephemera, and require different supernatural abilities to handle them. For example Mages uses the Mind Arcanum for Goetia and the Spirit Arcanum for Spirits.<br /> <br /> I hope that made sense. I haven't slept in 40 hours so I might've messed up some part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T23:49:08-07:00","id":1109642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1108754#post1108754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are not horrors actual Astral Spirits? The Primordial Dream exists in the Astral... &gt;.&gt;<br /> I'm just making a suggestion that hey.... What if that passage was a piece of Inspiration?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, there was a story in the Beast anthology that at one point had a mage making the point that Beasts are, in all likelihood, just another type of Astral possession, so maybe. Then again, mages have a tendency to overgeneralise for the sake of classification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T14:53:52-07:00","id":1109936,"title":"","content":"I can easily see Beasts as the Astral Realms' native inhabitants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T16:04:00-07:00","id":1109957,"title":"","content":"NOTE that I originally said Astral Spirit because of the previous post before mine (that I was responding to), and thought that the Astral's Ephemeral Entities or Goetia were being talked about. I Already knew that Spirits are from the Shadow and not the Astral.... And the moment that I was corrected, was the moment that I thought, are there Astral Spirits? Whats the difference? Sorry about my confusion....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T13:03:46-07:00","id":1110956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1109936#post1109936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can easily see Beasts as the Astral Realms' native inhabitants.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Goetia then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T21:23:26-07:00","id":1111142,"title":"","content":"I think they're something more primeval than goetia.<br /> <br /> That is to say, I'm not really comfortable defining beasts in terms of another game. I think a mage would most likely view a beast as goetia but I don't think that offers a complete or necessarily accurate summation of what a beast is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 07-04-2017, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T22:33:49-07:00","id":1111166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1111142#post1111142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're something more primeval than goetia.<br /> <br /> That is to say, I'm not really comfortable defining beasts in terms of another game. I think a mage would most likely view a beast as goetia but I don't think that offers a complete or necessarily accurate summation of what a beast is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if more primeval than what mages commonly experience, Horrors still count as Goetia because the very definition of &quot;Goetia&quot; is &quot;an ephemeral entity native to the Astral.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, you are on the spot with mages not having a complete summation on the nature of Horrors and the Primordial Dream. They're just well equipped to figure out such things, and even then they're on the outsider's perspective when studying them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T00:37:08-07:00","id":1111186,"title":"","content":"To me Beast's Horrors are to Goetia, like Idigam are to the Shadow Realm Sprits - <i>technically</i>, they are 'only' super weird version of normal spirits - <i>practically</i>, they are class of beings only vaguely related to main governing Arcana ( and similar powers - like both spirits and Idigam are under preview of Spirit Arcanum ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T01:05:37-07:00","id":1111188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1111186#post1111186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me Beast's Horrors are to Goetia, like Idigam are to the Shadow Realm Sprits - <i>technically</i>, they are 'only' super weird version of normal spirits - <i>practically</i>, they are class of beings only vaguely related to main governing Arcana ( and similar powers - like both spirits and Idigam are under preview of Spirit Arcanum ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Idigam are a bit extreme in the irregularity, I think. Rather, I'd compare Horrors and Geists. Both are types of ephemeral beings that display traits atypical of their fellows, the most prevalent one being that they can merge with a suitable human in a way that is specifically not a form of possession, which results in a gestalt entity that is neither fully mortal nor ephemeral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T05:06:05-07:00","id":1111209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1106479#post1106479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more interested about the material incarnation and &quot;hiding in the mortal world&quot; that some of those Chimericals attempt, since as of Mage 2e (and Beast), Goetia can't manifest by themselves in the waking world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts Incarnate can fill this niche, as well as Rampant for the more wild creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T05:55:51-07:00","id":1111220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1111209#post1111209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts Incarnate can fill this niche, as well as Rampant for the more wild creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose so, but Incarnates and Rampants don't seem to &quot;hide&quot; much, do they?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T06:15:16-07:00","id":1111228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1111188#post1111188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Idigam are a bit extreme in the irregularity, I think. Rather, I'd compare Horrors and Geists. Both are types of ephemeral beings that display traits atypical of their fellows, the most prevalent one being that they can merge with a suitable human in a way that is specifically not a form of possession, which results in a gestalt entity that is neither fully mortal nor ephemeral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, in 2E geists will specifically be a subset of ghosts where the only difference from regular ghosts is that they have the Bargain as a Manifestation.<br /> Horrors and regular goetia are a lot more different. I agree with Wyrd's analogue with spirits and idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T06:22:01-07:00","id":1111233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1111228#post1111228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, in 2E geists will specifically be a subset of ghosts where the only difference from regular ghosts is that they have the Bargain as a Manifestation.<br /> Horrors and regular goetia are a lot more different. I agree with Wyrd's analogue with spirits and idigam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm intrigued. Could you elaborate more on their similarities, other than both tapping into a primordial archetype? (You too, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, should you be interested!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T07:01:25-07:00","id":1111245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1111233#post1111233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I'm intrigued. Could you elaborate more on their similarities, other than both tapping into a primordial archetype? (You too, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, should you be interested!)</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about idigam is that they are spirits yet so unlike all other spirits. Horrors are by definition goetia, but they too are quite different from regular goetia. Other goetia feed on Resonances and the Temenotic variety inhabit different astral realms that are shaped by humanity rather than themselves. Horrors feed through their Beasts and inhabit Lairs that are shaped by their Beasts. The Primordial Dream is unique in the Temenos in that it's its own inhabitants that actually shape the Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T07:26:21-07:00","id":1111253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1103407-chimerical-beasts-in-secrets-of-the-ruined-temple?p=1111245#post1111245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about idigam is that they are spirits yet so unlike all other spirits. Horrors are by definition goetia, but they too are quite different from regular goetia. Other goetia feed on Resonances and the Temenotic variety inhabit different astral realms that are shaped by humanity rather than themselves. Horrors feed through their Beasts and inhabit Lairs that are shaped by their Beasts. The Primordial Dream is unique in the Temenos in that it's its own inhabitants that actually shape the Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another similarity between Horrors and idigam (because I like challenging my own arguments)- regular Goetia and spirits can't &quot;evolve&quot; into them. <br /> <br /> Continuing with my own arguments: Don't Beasts sating their Hungers count as providing Resonance? Isn't Beasts shaping their Lairs and thus the Primordial Dream a function of their human aspect, and not something a Horror by itself can do? (And thus, the rule that Goetia can't shape their own Astral realm is preserved?)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hey wait a second... do Goetia need to feed at all while in the Astral? If not, then at least that part of the debate is moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 07-04-2017, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}